/wildheart/contact"}}]},"retreat":{"root":{"props":{}},"content":[{"type":"PhotoHero","props":{"id":"wh-retreat-hero","variant":"image","display":"beside","image":"/brand/wildheart/photos/forest-witch.jpg","alt":"Tattooed hands and a fern pressed to a tree","eyebrow":"Samhain weekend · Oct 29 – 31, 2027","title":"The Wildheart *Retreat*","subtitle":"Three days on the thinnest night of the year, the same weekend as the Hearts on Fire Desert Retreat and held separately. Every circle together, in the wild dark.","actionPrimaryLabel":"Hold my place","actionPrimaryHref":"/spaces/wildheart/contact"}}]},"about":{"root":{"props":{}},"content":[{"type":"WildheartMarkSplit","props":{"id":"wh-about-mark","label":"About","heading":"A call to every woman who wants to be *free.*","lead":"Wildheart is the women''s branch of Hearth, a year-round circle and the sister to Hearts on Fire. It teaches women to come back into their bodies and let what is inside move out: in movement, voice, pleasure, play and presence. It is a place to take up space without apology.","body":"Wildheart is for women 25 to 55 who look capable from the outside and feel contained, tired or quietly disconnected from their own bodies and desires.","note":"Wildheart is practice and community, not therapy or crisis care. Every host has a written referral route for a woman who needs more than the circle can give."}}]}},"siteHero":{"eyebrow":"Women''s circles · Year-round · A Space on Frequency","heading":"For every woman who wants to be *free*.","tagline":"Wildheart is a year-round circle for women who are ready to stop holding it all together. Every other week you gather with the same women to move, breathe, make noise, laugh and feel at home in your body. Come once and see what wakes up.","action":{"label":"Come to one Circle Night","href":"/spaces/wildheart/circles"},"secondary":{"label":"How it works","href":"/spaces/wildheart/program"}},"coverScrim":"none","logoBackdrop":"none","profileData":{"about":"Wildheart is a year-round circle for women: 6 to 12 women and a trained host, meeting every other week, in person, through the seasons. Women come back into their bodies and let what is inside move out, through movement, voice, pleasure, play and presence. A place to take up space without apology.","offerings":[{"title":"Circle Night","blurb":"Every other week, in person, 90 minutes. Five beats: Presence, Unite, Lead, Settle, Exhale. Join in, go gently, witness or pass.","durationMinutes":90},{"title":"Year-round membership","blurb":"A full year: Circle Nights every other week, a daily practice you can keep, the eight-week Foundation, the eight festivals and every moon, the Samhain retreat, and a path to host your own circle."},{"title":"Wildheart Retreat","blurb":"Three nights in the wild dark on Samhain weekend. Every circle together, held apart from the Hearts on Fire Desert Retreat."}]},"profileLayout":{"rows":[{"id":"r0","columns":1,"cells":[["editorial","zigzag","cardGrid"]]},{"id":"r1","columns":1,"cells":[["offerings"]],"title":"Join","headerOn":true},{"id":"r2","columns":1,"cells":[["faq"]]},{"id":"r3","columns":1,"cells":[["accentBeat"]]},{"id":"r4","columns":2,"cells":[["contact"],["business"]],"title":"Contact and details","headerOn":true}],"content":{"about":{"eyebrow":"About","title":"About this space","body":"Wildheart is a year-round circle for women: 6 to 12 women and a trained host, meeting every other week, in person, through the seasons. Women come back into their bodies and let what is inside move out, through movement, voice, pleasure, play and presence. A place to take up space without apology."},"story":{"eyebrow":"About","title":"Our story","body":"Wildheart is a year-round circle for women: 6 to 12 women and a trained host, meeting every other week, in person, through the seasons. Women come back into their bodies and let what is inside move out, through movement, voice, pleasure, play and presence. A place to take up space without apology."},"editorial":{"eyebrow":"a year-round circle for women","title":"Wildheart","body":"Most women were taught to hold it all together: to look capable, stay contained, and keep everyone else going. Far fewer were taught to come back into their bodies and let what is inside move out.<br><br>Wildheart is a year of doing that together. You join a circle of 6 to 12 women and meet every other week. You move, breathe, make noise, laugh and feel at home in your body. It is not therapy. It is practice and community alongside other women."},"zigzag":{"title":"How it works","body":"Each Circle Night has five beats: Presence, Unite, Lead, Settle, Exhale. Every practice is an invitation. Join in, go gently, witness or pass.<br><br>The year follows the seasons and the twelve signs, from Sovereignty in Capricorn to Freedom in Sagittarius. The eight festivals and every moon fall inside it, and on Samhain weekend every circle gathers for the retreat.<br><br>Every woman starts with the same Foundation: eight self-guided weeks in breath, movement, sound, wanting and play, with your host checking in along the way.","mediaSide":"right","aspect":"vertical"},"cardGrid":{"eyebrow":"90 minutes, every other week","title":"A year of Circle Nights, festivals and moons, all in person.","subtitle":"Meet the same women, every season. Every circle is in the same sign at the same time.","columns":"2","shadow":false,"cards":[{"icon":"1","title":"Sisters","text":"Who know your name"},{"icon":"2","title":"Circle Night","text":"Every other Tuesday, 90 minutes, in person"},{"icon":"3","title":"A daily practice","text":"Breath, one song, a pause, three questions"},{"title":"The eight festivals and every moon","text":"Including the Samhain retreat"},{"title":"A path forward","text":"To host your own circle"}]},"offerings":{"items":["Circle Night","Year-round membership"]},"accentBeat":{"title":"Come to one Circle Night","body":"Join in, go gently, witness or pass.","buttonLabel":"Save my place","buttonUrl":"/spaces/wildheart"}}},"programOverview":"_Master overview, Oct 12, 2026. Daniel Tyack._\n\n## What Wildheart is\n\nWildheart is the women''s branch of Hearth, a year-round circle and the sister to Hearts on Fire: a call to every woman who wants to be free.\n\nWhere Hearts on Fire teaches men to turn inward and feel, Wildheart teaches women to come back into their bodies and let what is inside move out: in movement, voice, pleasure, play and presence. It is a place to take up space without apology. It runs on the same chassis as Hearts on Fire.\n\n- **The circles.** Small groups of 6 to 12 women who meet every other week, in person, all year.\n- **The meeting framework.** One repeatable rhythm for every gathering, simple enough for a new host to learn.\n- **The master curriculum.** Twelve modules that follow the four seasons and the twelve signs.\n- **The foundation course.** Eight self-guided weeks every member completes when she joins.\n\n> The program is built to grow by adding circles, not by making any one circle bigger. At 12 women, a circle seeds a new one.\n\n## The mirror\n\nThe two programs share one structure and point in opposite directions: Hearts on Fire moves men inward, Wildheart moves women outward.\n\n|  | Hearts on Fire | Wildheart |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| The call | Light up. Find the fire and carry it together. | Be free. Come home to your body and take up space. |\n| Direction | Inward: from doing and fixing to feeling | Outward: from holding and containing to expressing |\n| What they reclaim | Sensation, emotion, the right to slow down | Voice, appetite, pleasure, anger, the right to be seen |\n| Core practices | Stillness, breath, meditation, honest check-ins | Movement, breath, sound and voice, sensual awareness, play |\n| Energy of the room | Steady, contained, grounded | Alive, loud when it wants to be, warm |\n| Fire image | A flame that is tended and held | A wildfire that is allowed to burn |\n\n## Who it''s for\n\nWomen 25 to 55 who look capable from the outside and feel contained, tired or quietly disconnected from their own bodies and desires. What they want: to feel alive again, to be met by other women, to stop shrinking, and to enjoy their bodies and their lives. The gap is not having someone to talk to. It is having somewhere to stop holding everyone else and be fully themselves.\n\n| Need | Design response |\n| --- | --- |\n| A women-only space where they feel safe | Circles are women-only; safety and trust are stated, not assumed |\n| Choice and control | Every practice is an invitation; any woman can watch, modify or pass |\n| Somewhere to be the one who receives | Circle Night is the one place she is not hosting, managing or fixing |\n| Back into the body, out of the mirror | Practices focus on how the body feels, never how it looks |\n| Permission to move, sound and play | Movement is the core daily and in-room practice, not an add-on |\n\n## Structure on Frequency\n\nOne Space on Frequency, a primary circle, local circles, and shared events. Circles of 6 to 12 women and a trained host; at 12 a circle seeds a second one.\n\n## The member path\n\n1. **Visit.** Come to one Circle Night. Join in or simply witness.\n2. **Join.** Become a member of the Space and one circle.\n3. **Foundation.** Eight weeks, with check-ins from your host.\n4. **Practise.** A short daily practice and Circle Night.\n5. **Gather.** Hearth Gatherings and the Samhain retreat.\n6. **Host.** Train to co-lead or start a circle.\n\n## The foundation course\n\nEight self-guided weeks, Tuesdays at 6:00 PM from Jan 5 to Feb 23, 2027, with host check-ins. It mirrors the men''s intro, reversed in direction.\n\n| Week | Theme | Focus |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Arriving | Breath and noticing what the body feels, not how it looks |\n| 2 | Moving | Free movement and shaking; letting the body lead |\n| 3 | Sounding | Breath into sound, sighing, humming, the first loud note |\n| 4 | Wanting | Naming desire and appetite without apology |\n| 5 | No and yes | Boundaries in the body; a clear no makes a full yes possible |\n| 6 | Pleasure | Sensual awareness through the senses |\n| 7 | Fire | Anger and power as life force; moving it through |\n| 8 | Wild | Joy and play; choosing a practice to keep |\n\n_Daily practice, 20 to 30 minutes: breath, free movement to one song, a sensory pause, and three questions. Where do I feel alive right now? What do I want? What am I holding back?_\n\n## Circle Night, on the PULSE rhythm\n\nEvery Circle Night follows the same five beats, 90 minutes, every other week, in person. A woman can walk into any circle and know where she is.\n\n| Beat | In a Wildheart circle |\n| --- | --- |\n| Presence | Arrive in the body: breath, shaking, landing. |\n| Unite | A check-in round, each woman speaking and being witnessed. |\n| Lead | The module’s practice: movement, voice, ritual or teaching. |\n| Settle | Rest and integration, lying down, on the floor, quiet. |\n| Exhale | Close with sound, a commitment, and celebration. |\n\n## The four practice pillars\n\nEvery module draws on four pillars, so a woman builds the same capacities all year in different forms.\n\n- **Embodiment.** Feeling the body from inside, not watching it from outside.\n- **Sensuality.** Pleasure through the senses, at her own pace.\n- **Voice and expression.** Taking up space with sound, words and anger.\n- **Joy.** Play without purpose.\n\nSensuality, defined for this program: aliveness through the senses. Never sexual activity in the circle, never touch without explicit opt-in consent, never performance.\n\n## Master curriculum\n\nTwelve modules, one per sign, in four seasons, on the same calendar as Hearts on Fire so both circles are in the same sign at the same time. With Circle Night every other week, each module gets about two meetings.\n\n| Season | Sign | Starts | Wildheart module |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Winter | Capricorn | Dec 21 | Sovereignty: Your own authority, your own rules |\n| Winter | Aquarius | Jan 19 | Sisterhood: Being met without competing |\n| Winter | Pisces | Feb 18 | Flow: Tears, softness, letting it move |\n| Spring | Aries | Mar 20 | Rage: Anger as life force |\n| Spring | Taurus | Apr 20 | Pleasure: The senses, appetite, enough |\n| Spring | Gemini | May 20 | Voice: Sound, saying it out loud |\n| Summer | Cancer | Jun 21 | Mothers and daughters: Lineage, nurture, and what you will not pass on |\n| Summer | Leo | Jul 22 | Radiance: Being seen and taking up space |\n| Summer | Virgo | Aug 23 | Devotion: Caring for yourself as you care for others |\n| Fall | Libra | Sep 22 | Desire and boundaries: Yes, no, and asking |\n| Fall | Scorpio | Oct 23 | The Wild: The parts you were told to tame |\n| Fall | Sagittarius | Nov 22 | Freedom: The life you want, out loud |\n\n_Sign dates are approximate and should be computed for each year._\n\n## The year\n\nThe eight festivals of the Wheel of the Year (Imbolc, Ostara, Beltane, Litha, Lammas, Mabon, Samhain, Yule), a full moon circle to release and a new moon circle to plant every month, three Hearth Gatherings with Hearts on Fire, and the Wildheart Retreat on Samhain weekend, Oct 29 to 31, 2027: the same weekend as the Hearts on Fire Desert Retreat, held separately.\n\n## Consent, safety and care\n\nSensual and embodied work only feels free when it is safe, so safety is designed in, not left to the host''s instinct.\n\n- Women-only, led by women.\n- Every practice can be joined, modified, watched or skipped.\n- No touch between members unless a practice invites it and each woman opts in.\n- Nothing sexual happens in the circle.\n- No photos or recording of any practice.\n- What is shared stays in the circle.\n\nWildheart is practice and community, not therapy or crisis care. Hosts train in trauma-informed facilitation and hold a written referral route.\n\n## Voice and messaging\n\nWarm and bold, as an invitation: never a fix, never a sales pitch about what is wrong with her.\n\n| Use | Avoid |\n| --- | --- |\n| Free, alive, wild, whole, take up space, move, sound, joy, pleasure, sisters, circle | Fix, heal yourself, glow up, goddess cliches, \"too much\", body-shape language |\n| Invitation: come as you are, join in or witness | Pressure: \"break through\", \"transform in 8 weeks\" |\n| The body as felt from inside | Images that show bodies to be looked at |\n\n## Open decisions\n\n| Decision | Status |\n| --- | --- |\n| Who leads | Open. A woman as founding lead and primary circle host. |\n| Age range | Open. Keep 25 to 55, or open wider. |\n| Money | Open. Membership price, what hosts receive, how shared events are funded. |\n| Circle Night timing | Settled. Same Tuesdays as Hearts on Fire, 6 PM, every other week. |\n| Shared gatherings | Settled. Hearth Gatherings and a same-weekend retreat. |","siteFooter":{"columns":[{"title":"The program","links":[{"label":"How it works","href":"/spaces/wildheart/program"},{"label":"The sky map","href":"/spaces/wildheart/the-year"},{"label":"Samhain retreat","href":"/spaces/wildheart/retreat"}]},{"title":"Circles","links":[{"label":"Find a circle","href":"/spaces/wildheart/circles"},{"label":"Become a host","href":"/spaces/wildheart/circles"},{"label":"About","href":"/spaces/wildheart/about"}]},{"title":"On Frequency","links":[{"label":"The Wildheart Space","href":"/spaces/wildheart"},{"label":"Hearth Gatherings","href":"/spaces/wildheart/calendar"}]}],"blurb":"A year-round circle for women, run as one Space on Frequency with local circles that share a curriculum, a rhythm and a year.","line":"Women-only · Invitation, never instruction · No photos · What is shared stays here","note":"Practice and community, not therapy or crisis care.","suffix":"A program on Frequency"},"profilePublished":true}'::jsonb,
  updated_at = now()
where id = '5c7c46d1-a2ba-4e58-a942-c1fe6a68e74b';

-- Logo and cover: NOT set here (no URL is invented). The product stores both as public URLs in
-- the `library-media` storage bucket, under the Space id, as `<spaceId>/<unix ms>-<4 chars>.<ext>`
-- (Hearts on Fire: library-media/d9aa1c7b-.../1791407399184-kiuw.png, with a library_assets row and
-- spaces.brand_logo_asset_id pointing at it). The clean path is the product itself: upload
-- design_handoff_wildheart/assets/wildheart-logo.svg as the logo and one of assets/photos/*.jpg as the
-- cover through Manage > Branding (updateSpaceBranding writes brand_logo_url; the Loom uploader files
-- the library_assets row and brand_logo_asset_id). If you upload by hand instead, put the files at
--   library-media/5c7c46d1-a2ba-4e58-a942-c1fe6a68e74b/<unix ms>-<4 chars>.svg   (logo)
--   library-media/5c7c46d1-a2ba-4e58-a942-c1fe6a68e74b/<unix ms>-<4 chars>.jpg   (cover)
-- then run, with the real public URLs:
--   update spaces set brand_logo_url = '<LOGO_PUBLIC_URL>', cover_image_url = '<COVER_PUBLIC_URL>', updated_at = now() where id = '5c7c46d1-a2ba-4e58-a942-c1fe6a68e74b';
-- PLACEHOLDER: brand_logo_url, cover_image_url, brand_logo_asset_id stay as they are until then.

